CHAPTER.VERS:
And it will be a statute forever to you

          {+}
        : in the seventh month, on the tenth day of the month, you

          {+}
         will afflict your

          {+}
         souls, and will do no manner of work, the home-born, or the stranger who sojourns among you

          {+}
        :

for on this day atonement will be made for you

          {+}
        , to cleanse you

          {+}
        ; from all your

          {+}
         sins you

          {+}
         will be clean before Yahweh.

It is a Sabbath of solemn rest to you

          {+}
        , and you

          {+}
         will afflict your

          {+}
         souls; it is a statute forever.

And this will be an everlasting statute to you

          {+}
        , to make atonement for the sons of Israel because of all their sins once in the year. And he did as Yahweh commanded Moses.
